  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e749ce9f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: making_mashed_potatoes; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image shows a young child in a wheelchair on a beach, with the text 'making mashed potatoes' overlaid. This juxtaposition is likely intended to be humorous or ironic, implying the child is engaged in a mundane, domestic task while in a public, recreational setting. The meme may be perceived as harmful due to its potential to reinforce ableist stereotypes by portraying the child's disability as something to be mocked or trivialized, particularly by associating the child with a task typically associated with domestic labor or incompetence. The visual of a child in a wheelchair being paired with a domestic chore can unintentionally or intentionally infantilize or belittle the child's capabilities, which falls under the category of ableist toxicity. The meme does not contain direct abusive, cyberbullying, or hateful language, but the implication of the image-text combination can be interpreted as demeaning to individuals with physical disabilities, thus qualifying as harmful content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_3c811000"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
